    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nSherry FitzGerald are delighted to bring “Dunbrody” to the market. This charming bay fronted 1930's home has been sympathetically extended and refurbished over the years to create this wonderful family home. Whilst ready for immediate occupation Planning Permission granted in 2026 provides for further expansion allowing new owners the opportunity to further expand another 172sqm. Move into now and expand later or do it all at once the option is yours! \n\nSet back off Torquay Road enjoying a mature and exceptionally private site of approx. 0.3 acres with private, westerly orientation. The property enjoys well-appointed internal layout which is further enhanced by glass panelled doors, picture windows and the use of solid panelling to the walls creates a cosy intimate homely ambience. \n\nA delightful open porch with glazed roof and traditional wooden balustrade opens to the inviting hallway with tiled floor and panelled walls. Light streams in from the French doors at the back of the house and is reflected throughout with the use of glass panelled doors and large picture windows. \n\nThe reception rooms enjoy views out over the gardens and the kitchen, complete with AGA, is a bright and inviting family space in cool tones of blue and white. A utility room is located off the kitchen. \n\nDunbrody currently extends to approximately 2,200 sq.ft (204.38 sq.m) and is ready for immediate occupation. Refurbishment works carried out approximately 15 years ago include new windows, a new heating system, attractive tiled flooring in the hallway, newly fitted fireplace with stove inset in the family room and panelled walls in the hallway which continue to the first floor. Rising upstairs the first floor enjoys four spacious double bedrooms and a well-appointed bathroom complete with bath and separate shower. \n\nThe walls on the landing are panelled in keeping with the hallway downstairs and the overall pristine nature of this very fine home. \n\nThe great feature is however that Planning permission also exists to extend the house with a combination of a single story extension to the west and a two story extension to the east gable adding a total of 172sqm. Plans have been drawn up by DMVF Architects. Planning Reference D25A/0901/WEB. \n\nHaving been well maintained over the years, Dunbrody is a turnkey family home offering both immediate comfort and long-term potential. With planning permission already secured, purchasers have the opportunity to move in and enjoy the property from day one while considering a future extension to create their ideal home.\n\nThe location is second to none, only a short stroll from the charming and bustling village of Foxrock with its cafes, boutiques and restaurants and indeed within walking distance to The Leopardstown Inn and a selection of shops in Leopardstown. There are excellent transport links close by at the M50, LUAS stop at Sandyford & Carrickmines and N11 which offers ease of access to the city centre and the popular QBC. For sports enthusiasts you have Carrickmines Lawn Tennis & Croquet Club, Westwood fitness centre, Foxrock and Carrickmines Golf Clubs and Leopardstown Race course. Other amenities include shops, boutiques and restaurants. Extensive shopping facilities are nearby at Cornelscourt, Stillorgan, Blackrock, Dundrum and Carrickmines Retail Park. There is a wide selection of National and Secondary schools close by to include the Nord Anglia International school located just moments away in Leopardstown. Viewing is highly recommended to fully appreciate such a beautiful home with the gardens to match.\n\nGarden \nThe grounds which extend to 0.3 acres approximately are incredibly private. A gravelled driveway provides parking for several cars. Neatly laid cobble stones punctuate the driveway providing structure and delineates the garden zones. \n\nWide side garden in lawn with mature trees and shrubs providing total privacy and creating a sun-drenched oasis enjoying the perfect westerly orientation. \n\nThe garden is bordered with mature tress and colourful planting with a paved patio area for daylong sunshine with direct access from the hall and the kitchen/breakfast room downstairs. Garage. Barna hut."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nOpen Porch - \nwith glazed roof and traditional wooden balustrade leads to the hall door\n\nEntrance Hall - \nA mosaic tiled floor echoing the 1930s style. Paneled walls. French doors to rear patio.\n\nFamily Room - \nwith feature bay window, marble fireplace and built-in wood burning stove.\n\nLiving Room - \nFeature open marble fireplace. Opens to:\n\nDining Room - \nDual aspect with large picture windows overlooking the gardens to the back and side. Glass paneled wall and door to hallway.\n\nKitchen/Breakfast Room - \nWhite Miele kitchen with extensively fitted wall and floor units. Corian worktops and Amtico floor. Miele cooker with 4 plate gas hob. Gas fired Aga. Dining area with vaulted white painted ceiling. Sliding doors to patio area to the back.\n\nUtility Room - \nCeramic Belfast sink. Fitted shelving. “Ideal Logic Heat 30”. Door to garden.WC: with whb, wc\n\nFirst Floor - \n\n\nBedroom 1 - \nDouble bedroom to the rear overlooking gardens. Built in wardrobes.\n\nBedroom 2 - \nDouble bedroom. Feature bay window. Built-in wardrobes\n\nBedroom 3 - \nDouble bedroom overlooking rear garden, built in wardrobes.\n\nBedroom 4 - \nDouble bedroom with dual aspect. Floor to ceiling, Hot press with shelving.\n\nBathroom - \nwith bath, whb in vanity unit, wc, bidet and separate shower with Triton Electric shower.\n\n"
      },
